        "original_id": "0999e5ff-b6a6-511d-a944-7cf502c268e5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Nostalgia (2018 film)\n- People: Mark Pellington, Alex Ross Perry, Patton Oswalt, Jon Hamm, Nick Offerman, Amber Tamblyn, Catherine Keener, Ellen Burstyn, Bruce Dern, John Ortiz, James LeGros\n- Topics: American drama films, stand-up comedy, acting, voice acting, writing\n\nFacts:\n- Patton Peter Oswalt was born on January 27, 1969, and he is an American stand-up comedian, actor, voice actor, and writer.\n- Patton Oswalt is known for playing Spencer Olchin in the sitcom The King of Queens from 1998 to 2007.\n- Patton Oswalt voiced Remy in the 2007 film Ratatouille.\n- Patton Oswalt played multiple identical brothers, the Koenigs, on Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. from 2014 to 2017.\n- Patton Oswalt voiced male Jesse in both seasons of Minecraft: Story Mode.\n- Nostalgia is an upcoming American drama film directed by Mark Pellington and written by Mark Pellington and Alex Ross Perry.\n- Nostalgia stars Jon Hamm, Nick Offerman, Amber Tamblyn, Patton Oswalt, Catherine Keener, Ellen Burstyn, Bruce Dern, John Ortiz, and James LeGros.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
